+
+| Item | Sev | Finding | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| owner report 2026-11-05 | high | 305 installed skills filled a 64K window on step 1; at bounded size the catalog is names only | FIXED. Catalog stays bounded (PR #409); per-prompt `[Nexus skill note]` (up to 5 descriptions, 2% of the window) follows each operator message and stays where written; system prompt byte-identical across turns. Commit `feat(cli): per-prompt skill note after the operator message`; tests `a prompt naming a skill's domain gets that skill's description immediately after that message`, `an unrelated prompt gets no note`, `across two operator messages the second request starts with the first request's messages unchanged`, `the system prompt is byte-identical across turns with different prompts`, `the note stays inside its budget when 40 skills match, and a 305-skill host starts without a capacity block` |
+| WP-1308 lookup | medium | Model chooses a skill by name alone once the catalog is names only | FIXED. `activate_skill` searches when no skill has the name (no new tool, no schema weight beyond one description sentence). Commit `feat(cli): activate_skill searches when no skill has that name`; tests `a query that is no skill's name returns ranked matches and activates nothing`, `an exact name still activates, and a query nothing matches says so without listing every skill`; untrusted never scored: `untrusted workspace skills are never scored` |
+| #409 review | low | Pre-#409 saved session keeps the full catalog in `messages[0]` and stays blocked on resume | FIXED. Commit `fix(cli): skill catalog re-size recognises pre-#409 sessions...`; test `a session saved before PR #409 keeps no full catalog: it is recognised by its heading and cut to the window` |
+| #409 review | low | `resizeSkillCatalog` recorded the new catalog even when the old text was not found | FIXED. Same commit; test `a recorded catalog is replaced only when it was found; a miss is not recorded` |
+| #409 review | low | A catalog that shrank to nothing cannot come back | FIXED by decision: it stays absent (notes and lookup cover those windows; rewriting `messages[0]` drops the prefix cache). Test `a catalog that shrank to nothing stays absent: notes and lookup cover it` |
+| #409 review | low | `getPromptSection` built the final listing twice | FIXED. Same commit as the resume fix (built once, in a variable) |
+| #409 review | low | First-discovery condition and resume path tested only through a full turn | FIXED. Tests `first discovery re-sizes once, directly` and the resume test above call `resizeSkillCatalog` directly |
+| #409 review | low | `activate_skill` not-found error listed every skill name; catalog hint said so | FIXED. Lookup commit; the hint now reads "pass words describing the task to `activate_skill` to search them" (`tighter budgets shorten descriptions, then list names, then count the rest`) |
+| WP-1308 review | medium | A note after a very large operator message would turn it into an earlier request that compaction may condense instead of refusing the turn | FIXED (found while testing). A message taking a quarter of the window gets no note; tests `a message too large for the window gets no note, so the turn is still refused and withdrawn whole`, `a turn refused after its note was written withdraws the note with the message` |
15:**Numbering.** `WP-1301` to `WP-1308`, `WP-1310` to `WP-1316` below are the v1.1.4 work packages. They supersede the same IDs in `docs/v1.1.0/ROADMAP.md` (OTLP exporter, provenance graph, macOS builds, knowledge freshness, cgroup limits, Composio mesh), which were never scheduled. Those roadmap items keep their own IDs only inside that document; in commits, claims and findings, `WP-13xx` means this plan. If one of them is scheduled later, give it a new ID.
